From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:38:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rk3399: the LPDDR4 timing set of the Rigol boards,
 from the scope's own controller values

Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

NOVA_RK3399_DDR_RIGOL (off) gives the TPL a timing set made for these
boards' two CXMT CXDB4CBAM parts, field by field from what the scope's
own first stage leaves in the controller, read from a running scope as
a register dump:

- rk3399-sdram-lpddr4-rigol.dtsi: the boot copy (CTL F2, PI P0) and
  the 856 MHz copy (CTL F1, PI P1) hold the scope's values; the 400 MHz
  training copy (CTL F0, PI P2) is the generic one with tRFCab 280 ns
  (8 Gb per channel), tXSR/tXSNR tRFCab + 7.5 ns and tRAS(max)
  9 x tREFI from the CXDB4CBAM datasheet, which the generic set
  undercuts (180 ns, 137.5 ns, 70 us); the boot copy takes the
  scope's tXSR/tXSNR (287.5 ns) with the rest of it.
- sdram-rk3399-lpddr4-856-rigol.inc: the final rate is 856 MHz, the
  scope's own, with its per-rate PHY values (read pointer update 6,
  gate latency start 2, tCKSRE wait 4).
- above the boot rate the drive, termination and Vref are the scope's
  (the generic 933 MHz entry's values) from the 400 MHz training on,
  with the DRAM pull-up calibrated to VDDQ/2.5 (MR3 OP[0] 0) and the
  read termination in PHY_925[7:0], as the scope's.
- PHY_TCKSRE_WAIT and PHY_CAL_CLK_SELECT_0 follow each rate's copy.

Generated field by field from that register dump; the
generic path is unchanged when the option is off.

Signed-off-by: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
---
 arch/arm/dts/rk3399-nova-rigol-u-boot.dtsi    |    4 +
 arch/arm/dts/rk3399-sdram-lpddr4-rigol.dtsi   | 1549 ++++++++++++++++
 board/rigol/nova_rk3399/Kconfig               |   17 +
 .../sdram-rk3399-lpddr4-856-rigol.inc         | 1590 +++++++++++++++++
 drivers/ram/rockchip/sdram_rk3399.c           |   61 +-
 5 files changed, 3218 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/dts/rk3399-sdram-lpddr4-rigol.dtsi
 create mode 100644 drivers/ram/rockchip/sdram-rk3399-lpddr4-856-rigol.inc

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-nova-rigol-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-nova-rigol-u-boot.dtsi
index d33ead88..c7342261 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-nova-rigol-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-nova-rigol-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -16,8 +16,12 @@
 
 #include "rk3399-u-boot.dtsi"
 #ifdef CONFIG_NOVA_RK3399_MAINLINE
+#ifdef CONFIG_NOVA_RK3399_DDR_RIGOL
+#include "rk3399-sdram-lpddr4-rigol.dtsi"
+#else
 #include "rk3399-sdram-lpddr4-100.dtsi"
 #endif
+#endif
 
 / {
 	aliases {
diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-sdram-lpddr4-rigol.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-sdram-lpddr4-rigol.dtsi
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..af9b86ab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-sdram-lpddr4-rigol.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,1549 @@
